 "name": "guest_clock",
 "doc": "The guest clock and why it stands still (nxnative hle_os.c guest_clock_freeze_for). The state IS the reason set: its number is the bit mask (bit 0 Hold: a test or loading-screen hold, bit 1 Background: the app is not in focus, bit 2 Keyboard: the system keyboard is up), so one read of the state is one consistent snapshot. The clock runs only in Running, which carries the lag (host ns minus guest ns); every other state carries the guest ns it is frozen at. Freezing a reason that already holds and thawing one that does not are transitions to the same state.",
